        "description": "Exactly three printed equivalences, one per line, stacked in this order: 1 day = 24 hours, 1 hour = 60 minutes, 1 minute = 60 seconds. The source writes the first as '1 day-and-night has 24 hours'; the modern edition states the same equality as 1 day = 24 h.",
